  "lessons": [
    {
      "key": "what-is-gen-ai",
      "name": "What is Generative AI?",
      "absolute_position": 1,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "Students will be introduced to generative artificial intelligence (AI), understanding what it is and seeing examples of its capabilities, such as creating text, images, and other media. They will explore common applications of generative AI in everyday life and discuss the general idea of how these systems produce novel outputs. By the end, students should be able to identify and describe various generative AI tools."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "what-is-gen-ai",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "how-gen-ai-learns",
      "name": "How Generative AI Learns Patterns",
      "absolute_position": 2,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "This lesson delves into the fundamental mechanism behind generative AI: pattern-based prediction. Students will learn that generative AI systems analyze massive datasets to identify statistical patterns and probabilities, which they then use to predict the most likely next word, pixel, or element. They will understand how these predictions accumulate to form coherent text or images."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "how-gen-ai-learns",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "training-data-impact",
      "name": "The Role of Training Data",
      "absolute_position": 3,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "Students will explore how the quality and characteristics of training data directly influence what a generative AI model can produce and where its outputs might fall short. They will learn that AI models are only as good as the data they are trained on, and how biases or limitations in the dataset can lead to inaccurate, unfair, or incomplete results. By the end, students should recognize that training data shapes an AI's capabilities and failures."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "training-data-impact",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "gen-ai-limitations",
      "name": "Limitations of Generative AI",
      "absolute_position": 4,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "This lesson focuses on the inherent limitations of generative AI, such as hallucination (generating false information), confidence calibration (expressing high confidence in incorrect outputs), and gaps due to insufficient or biased training data. Students will learn to critically evaluate generative AI outputs and understand that these tools lack true understanding or intent. They will practice identifying common pitfalls in AI-generated content."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "gen-ai-limitations",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "intro-classification-ai",
      "name": "Introduction to Classification AI",
      "absolute_position": 5,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "Students will be introduced to classification AI models and understand how they differ from generative AI. They will learn that classification models are designed to categorize data into predefined groups, such as identifying objects in images or sentiments in text, based on patterns learned from labeled training data. By the end, students should be able to distinguish between generative and classification AI and provide examples of classification tasks."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "intro-classification-ai",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "problem-solving-approaches",
      "name": "Choosing the Right Problem-Solving Approach",
      "absolute_position": 6,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "This lesson teaches students to differentiate between procedural instructions, rule-based logic, and data-informed models (like AI classification) as methods for solving problems. They will analyze various scenarios and justify which approach is most appropriate, considering factors like complexity, predictability, and the availability of data. By the end, students should be able to decide whether a problem is best solved with traditional algorithms or an AI model."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "problem-solving-approaches",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "planning-ai-program",
      "name": "Planning Your AI Program",
      "absolute_position": 7,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "Students will learn to plan block-based programs that integrate an AI classification model. They will use tools like flowcharts or pseudocode to outline the program's logic, focusing on how the AI model's input and output will fit into the overall structure. This lesson emphasizes decomposition and structuring a program before coding, considering the AI as a functional component."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "planning-ai-program",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "integrate-classification-ai",
      "name": "Integrating Classification AI into a Program",
      "absolute_position": 8,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "Students will build a simple block-based program that incorporates a pre-trained AI classification model. They will learn how to send input to the AI model and receive its output, making it a functional part of their program. This lesson focuses on the practical steps of calling an AI service within their coding environment."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "integrate-classification-ai",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "respond-ai-outputs",
      "name": "Responding to AI Outputs: Conditionals & Loops",
      "absolute_position": 9,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "This lesson teaches students how to make their programs react intelligently to the outputs of an AI classification model. Students will use conditional statements (if/else) to implement different behaviors based on the AI's classification and loops to process multiple AI outputs or retries. They will also consider scenarios where the AI model might be incorrect and how the program should handle such instances."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "respond-ai-outputs",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "handle-ai-errors",
      "name": "Handling AI Model Errors and Uncertainty",
      "absolute_position": 10,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "Students will explore strategies for building more robust AI-powered programs by anticipating and managing model errors or uncertain predictions. They will learn techniques like setting confidence thresholds, offering alternative actions, or prompting user clarification when the AI's output is low-confidence or potentially wrong. This lesson emphasizes designing for resilience and user experience in the face of AI imperfections."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "handle-ai-errors",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ai-programming-tutor",
      "name": "Working with an AI Programming Tutor",
      "absolute_position": 11,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "Students will interact with a generative AI tool designed to assist with programming tasks, such as generating code snippets, debugging, or explaining concepts. They will practice formulating clear prompts and providing sufficient context to get helpful responses from the AI tutor. The goal is to learn how to effectively use AI as a supportive programming resource."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "ai-programming-tutor",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "evaluate-ai-tutor",
      "name": "Critically Evaluating AI Tutor Responses",
      "absolute_position": 12,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 12,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "Building on their understanding of generative AI limitations, students will learn to critically evaluate the outputs of their AI programming tutor. They will identify potential issues like hallucinated code, incomplete explanations, or unhelpful suggestions. Students will develop skills to discern when to accept, revise, or reject the AI's advice, fostering a skeptical but informed approach to using AI assistants."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "evaluate-ai-tutor",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "user-centered-ai-design",
      "name": "User-Centered Design for AI Programs",
      "absolute_position": 13,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 13,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "This lesson focuses on designing AI-powered programs with the end-user in mind. Students will learn to evaluate whether their program genuinely serves its target audience, considering factors beyond just functionality, such as fairness, usability, and potential negative impacts. They will identify areas where the AI model's outputs might fall short for real users and brainstorm improvements."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "user-centered-ai-design",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "test-debug-improve-ai",
      "name": "Testing, Debugging, and Improving AI Programs",
      "absolute_position": 14,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 14,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "Students will engage in an iterative process of testing, debugging, and refining their AI-powered programs. They will learn strategies for identifying when the AI model is performing poorly or causing unexpected program behavior. Through systematic testing and user feedback, students will modify their code and consider adjusting their AI integration to enhance performance and user satisfaction."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "test-debug-improve-ai",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ai-real-world-ethics",
      "name": "AI's Real-World Impact and Ethical Considerations",
      "absolute_position": 15,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 15,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "This lesson examines the broader societal implications of AI, focusing on how design decisions made when building AI-powered products in the real world have significant consequences for users. Students will discuss ethical issues, biases, and the potential for both beneficial and harmful impacts of AI algorithms, connecting their own design choices to real-world scenarios."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "ai-real-world-ethics",
        "lesson_group.key": "outlines",
        "script.name": "sample-aid-sc2-unit-generation"
      }
    }
  ],
